      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_961c6eb1",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person with a shaved head, likely representing a chemotherapy patient, juxtaposed with text that is sexually explicit and degrading. The text suggests a harmful and exploitative attitude toward individuals undergoing cancer treatment, implying that their illness makes them sexually available or that their condition is a justification for sexual acts. This is deeply insensitive and potentially harmful, as it trivializes the suffering of cancer patients and normalizes sexual exploitation of vulnerable individuals. The meme uses the visual of a patient to reinforce a grotesque and degrading message, which can cause emotional harm to those who see it or are part of the affected community. The overall intent is to shock or provoke through vulgar humor, but it does so at the expense of human dignity and medical ethics.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
